  "id": "COMPOUND:27025 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Hypocrellol B appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to SCCH-26, suggesting a complex interaction between the compound and the cell line. The evidence indicates that Hypocrellol B may act through CDK3/cyclin E, which is targeted by GlyTouCan:G99562EF and Vatalbinoside C, both of which also target SCCH-26. SGI-1776, a known inhibitor of P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1, is also targeted by Hypocrellol B, further supporting a potential mechanism involving this receptor. The integration of these pathways suggests that Hypocrellol B may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately modulate SCCH-26's activity. The overlapping targets and the shared downstream effect on SCCH-26 imply a possible functional link, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
